Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> A potion of ink can be quaffed to become visible or thrown at an invisible
> monster to make them visible again.
>
> If one dips a magic marker into a potion of ink, it will recharge the
> marker.

It's a good idea, when posting YANIs, to put those letters in the
subject line, so newbies won't think the item is actually in the
game....

Two of the most recent potions added to the game have been "utility"
potions, Oil and Acid, so Ink would fit in.  I like the idea of potions
that don't have drinking as their primary attribute, too.

There is the question, however, of whether this makes magic markers
over-powered.  Note that currently markers can be recharged only once.
Would a potion of ink let the player out of that?  How much should it
recharge the marker?

In any case, this YANI doesn't seem like it would be that difficult to
implement.  It would require a new item state perhaps, Dipped in Ink or
maybe alternatively Inky.  Let's think like the Dev Team for a moment:
from what other items would the player benefit if they were dipped in
ink?  (Not scrolls, for sure.)  How about written on?

